about areset asynchronous positive edge. \"positive edge triggered asynchronous resetting\" means reset when areset=1, asynchronous. Sensitivity list posedge clk or posedge areset. If areset is level? \"positive edge triggered asynchronous resetting\" means reset on posedge areset, asynchronous. But typical HDLBits uses `always @(posedge clk or posedge areset) if (areset)`. Yes.\n\nNeed ensure next state logic and counter. We can do one always for state and cnt, or combinational next + sequential. To avoid issues with counter, can compute next_cnt in combinational.\n\nLet's write:\n\n```systemverilog\nmodule TopModule(\n    input clk,\n    input areset,\n    input bump_left,\n    input bump_right,\n    input ground,\n    input dig,\n    output walk_left,\n    output walk_right,\n    output aaah,\n    output digging\n);\n\n    localparam LEFT   = 3'd0,\n               RIGHT  = 3'd1,\n               FALL_L = 3'd2,\n               FALL_R = 3'd3,\n               DIG_L  = 3'd4,\n               DIG_R  = 3'd5,\n               SPLAT  = 3'd6;\n\n    reg [2:0] state, next_state;\n    reg [4:0] cnt, next_cnt;\n\n    // State transition logic\n    always @(*) begin\n        next_state = state;\n        next_cnt = cnt;\n        case (state)\n            LEFT: begin\n                if (!ground) begin\n                    next_state = FALL_L;\n                    next_cnt = 5'd1;\n                end else if (dig) begin\n                    next_state = DIG_L;\n                end else if (bump_left) begin\n                    next_state = RIGHT;\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = LEFT;\n                end\n            end\n            RIGHT: begin\n                if (!ground) begin\n                    next_state = FALL_R;\n                    next_cnt = 5'd1;\n                end else if (dig) begin\n                    next_state = DIG_R;\n                end else if (bump_right) begin\n                    next_state = LEFT;\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = RIGHT;\n                end\n            end\n            DIG_L: begin\n                if (!ground) begin\n                    next_state = FALL_L;\n                    next_cnt = 5'd1;\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = DIG_L;\n                end\n            end\n            DIG_R: begin\n                if (!ground) begin\n                    next_state = FALL_R;\n                    next_cnt = 5'd1;\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = DIG_R;\n                end\n            end\n            FALL_L: begin\n                if (ground) begin\n                    if (cnt > 5'd20) begin\n                        next_state = SPLAT;\n                        next_cnt = 5'd0;\n                    end else begin\n                        next_state = LEFT;\n                        next_cnt = 5'd0;\n                    end\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = FALL_L;\n                    if (cnt < 5'd21)\n                        next_cnt = cnt + 5'd1;\n                    else\n                        next_cnt = cnt;\n                end\n            end\n            FALL_R: begin\n                if (ground) begin\n                    if (cnt > 5'd20) begin\n                        next_state = SPLAT;\n                        next_cnt = 5'd0;\n                    end else begin\n                        next_state = RIGHT;\n                        next_cnt = 5'd0;\n                    end\n                end else begin\n                    next_state = FALL_R;\n                    if (cnt < 5'd21)\n                        next_cnt = cnt + 5'd1;\n                    else\n                        next_cnt = cnt;\n                end\n            end\n            SPLAT: begin\n                next_state = SPLAT;\n                next_cnt = 5'd0;\n            end\n            default: begin\n                next_state = LEFT;\n                next_cnt = 5'd0;\n            end\n        endcase\n    end\n\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge areset) begin\n        if (areset) begin\n            state <= LEFT;\n            cnt <= 5'd0;\n        end else begin\n            state <= next_state;\n            cnt <= next_cnt;\n        end\n    end\n\n    assign walk_left = (state == LEFT);\n    assign walk_right = (state == RIGHT);\n    assign aaah = (state == FALL_L) || (state == FALL_R);\n    assign digging = (state == DIG_L) || (state == DIG_R);\n\nendmodule\n```\n\nNeed check if counter behavior aligns with \"falls for more than 20 clock cycles\". Let's test edge cases. Suppose state LEFT, ground=0 at posedge1. next_state=FALL_L, next_cnt=1. At posedge1, state becomes FALL_L, cnt=1. This means after edge1, output aaah=1. The first falling cycle is between edge1 and edge2. At posedge2, if ground=1, then in FALL_L, cnt=1. Since cnt >20? no, next_state=LEFT, cnt=0. So it was in FALL_L for one cycle. That's fall of 1 clock cycle. If ground=0 at posedge2, next_cnt=2, state stays FALL_L. So after edge2, cnt=2. The second falling cycle is between edge2 and edge3. At posedge3, if ground=1, cnt=2. It was in FALL for two cycles. So cnt equals number of completed falling cycles. If ground=1 at posedge N+1, cnt=N. Splatter if N>20. So fall >20 cycles means N>=21. Our check cnt>20. Correct.\n\nWhat about initial cycle when ground=0 and state LEFT: at posedge1, we sample ground=0, transition to FALL. The cycle between posedge1 and posedge2 is first falling cycle. At posedge2, if ground=1, cnt=1, resumes walk. So fall lasted 1 cycle. Good.\n\nWhat if ground=0 for exactly 20 cycles then ground=1: at posedge after 20 cycles, cnt=20, check >20 false -> walk. Good.\n\nWhat if ground=0 for 21 cycles: cnt=21, check >20 true -> splat. Good.\n\nNow, subtlety: \"being bumped in the same cycle as ground disappears (but not yet falling), or when the ground reappears while still falling, also does not affect the walking direction